  "catalog": {
    "slug": "library-checkout",
    "title": "Library Checkout",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "author": "simetro",
    "description": "Returned books in the bin, holds racked, patrons at the desk. Keep the queue calm and the new-release shelf full before the after-school stampede.",
    "tags": [
      "sl1",
      "scenario_language_v1",
      "showcase",
      "daily_life",
      "tutorial"
    ],
    "palette_note": "Parchment cream on ink black; library-stamp crimson, leather-spine ochre, fern green for fines paid, ink blue for holds, lavender for the children's hour.",
    "layout_note": "Return bin (source) feeds the sorting cart (compute_cluster), processed books reach the new-release shelf (dashboard), and a reference librarian overlay (operator) watches the floor.",
    "node_language_note": "source / compute_cluster / dashboard / operator. Compute_cluster is the sorting cart; the dashboard is the public-facing shelf.",
    "mover_path_note": "Movers do not exist yet for SL1 scenes; the legacy pieces.movers array is intentionally empty. SL1 links from return-bin to sorting-cart to new-release-shelf represent typed book flow; sort-and-shelve and rack-hold run on sorting-cart, checkout-patron runs on new-release-shelf. Cross-place transport surfaces as movers when the SL1 renderer ships.",
    "review_note": "Marked status=draft in the frontend catalog because the SL1 canvas renderer is not yet wired. Selecting this scene loads it successfully and shows catalog metadata in the scene browser. The SL1 HUD chips, dashboard freshness pill, and milestone strip render via the existing SL1 HUD overlay; the bespoke canvas vignette ships when the SL1 renderer is wired in a later PR."
  },
